<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    French card-shape markers. See values/arrays.xml for what these are
    and for the "a localized array replaces the default wholesale" rule
    that is why the English entry is repeated here.

    UNVERIFIED: "Sponsorisé" is the label Google uses for ads across its
    French interfaces, but it has not been captured from a real
    French-locale Google TV by this project. It only ever makes a banner be
    ignored, so a wrong guess costs nothing - it just never matches.

    KNOWN GAP, deliberate: no French equivalent of title_markers,
    youtube_markers, the subscription phrases or
    voice_search_detail_page_labels has been captured, so those are left
    undefined and fall back to the English defaults, which will never match
    French launcher text. French movie/show detection therefore rests on the
    locale-agnostic structural fallbacks (android.view.View + a
    comma-separated content-desc in isMovieOrShowCard, and the hero-banner
    shape in extractHeroTitle) - the same ones that carry Danish.

    To close the gap: on a French Google TV, click a price/rating card, a
    subscription-gated card and an ad banner with
    "adb logcat -s ReelyRelay:D" running, read the real content-desc out of
    the "Click event:" log line, and add the real markers here. Do not
    guess them.
-->
<resources>

    <string-array name="sponsored_labels">
        <item>Sponsorisé</item>
        <item>Sponsored</item>
    </string-array>

</resources>
